## Phase 3 definition of done

Phase 3 is complete when all of the following are true:

```text
Reset MCU
	↓
Initialize deterministic SRAM
	↓
Load encoded 16-bit instructions into Flash
	↓
Fetch and decode LD/ST through avr_mcu_step
	↓
Form X from R27:R26
	↓
Read/write bounded SRAM
	↓
Update registers without changing SREG
	↓
Advance PC only after successful execution
```

The emulator must be able to run a tiny encoded program that stores a value
from a register to SRAM and loads it back into another register. Valid memory
operations must work at the lowest and highest supported SRAM addresses.
Invalid addresses and unsupported instructions must fail without partial
state mutation. All Phase 1 and Phase 2 tests must remain green under the
existing strict-warning build.

### Explicitly out of scope

- `PORTB`, `DDRB`, `PINB`, or any GPIO behavior
- `IN`, `OUT`, `SBI`, or other I/O instructions
- AVR register-file and I/O-space memory aliases
- Y and Z pointer addressing
- Displacement, pre-decrement, or post-increment addressing
- `LDS`, `STS`, or any 32-bit instruction
- Branches, loops, calls, returns, or stack behavior
- Stack pointer implementation
- Interrupts, timers, UART, SPI, I2C, EEPROM, and cycle timing
- ELF, Intel HEX, assembler, or other binary loading
- GUI or visualizer work
- Full ATmega328P SRAM sizing or complete data-memory fidelity
- Broad cleanup of existing null-handling or public API behavior

The key achievement of Phase 3 is that the emulator now has a real, bounded
data-memory path: **machine code → instruction → X pointer → SRAM → register**.
